<title>USA: Tatham Offshore Inc Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Tatham Offshore Inc Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Unaudited)</p>
<p>			  For the Three Months  For the Nine Months</p>
<p>				     Ended March 31,  Ended March 31,</p>
<p>				    1997	1996	1997     1996</p>
<p> Oil and gas revenue	$ 6,206   $ 5,900  $16,508  $11,109</p>
<p>Production and operating</p>
<p>  expenses			2,609     2,313    6,037   11,068</p>
<p> Exploration expenses	    47	 101	375	333</p>
<p>General and administrative</p>
<p>  expenses			1,412     1,478    3,950    5,456</p>
<p>Depreciation and depletion</p>
<p>				    1,359	 460    3,500	840</p>
<p> Total operating expense    5,427     4,352   13,862   17,697</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)	779     1,548    2,646  (6,588)</p>
<p> Gain on sale of assets	 ---    11,322	---   22,641</p>
<p>Net interest expense and other</p>
<p>				  (1,899)   (2,207)  (5,892)  (6,213)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	  (1,120)    10,663  (3,246)    9,840</p>
<p> Preferred stock dividends  (970)     (112)  (2,944)    (112)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) available</p>
<p>  to common shareholders  (2,090)    10,551  (6,190)    9,728</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share</p>
<p>				   (0.08)	0.33   (0.23)     0.36</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  shares outstanding	 26,892    31,790   26,444   27,268</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for the three months ended March 31, 1996, included a gain of $11.3 million which represented the recognition of the remaining 50 percent of the gain attributable to the sale of working intersts in three offshore properties to Flextrend Development Co, L.L.C.</p>
<p>Net loss for three months ended March 31 totaled $2.1 million, or $0.08 per share, after allowing for $1.0 million in preferred stock dividends, as compared with net income of $10.6 million, or $0.33 per share after allowing for $0.1 million in preferred stock dividends for the year-ago period.</p>
<p>The company's net loss for the nine months ended March 31 totaled $6.2 million, or $0.23 per share, after allowing for $2.9 million in preferred stock dividends, as compared with net income available to common hsareholders of $9.7 million, or $0.36 per share, after allowing for $0.1 million in preferred stock dividends for the year-ago period.</p>
